          "text": "Dear Colleague,\n\nHistory of Present Illness:\nThe patient has focal epilepsy with onset at 28 years of age. Seizures are focal impaired-awareness seizures occurring approximately once per month. The epilepsy has a genetic etiology associated with a PCDH19 c.918G>A variant and is drug-resistant.\n\nCurrent Antiseizure Medications:\n- Valproate\n- Brivaracetam\n- Perampanel\n\nSeizure Burden:\nApproximately one focal impaired-awareness seizure per month.\n\nAssessment:\nDrug-resistant focal epilepsy with focal impaired-awareness seizures, of genetic etiology due to the PCDH19 c.918G>A variant.\n\nPlan:\nContinue the current antiseizure medication regimen of valproate, brivaracetam, and perampanel. Continue monitoring seizure frequency.",
